the principal of example_loan is a money if
    the USD for 25000 is the money.

the monthly rate for a terms is a number N if
    the annual interest rate of the terms is a number M
    and N = M / 12.

the power for a base B with an exp E is a number N if
    0 is equal to E
    and N is equal to 1
    otherwise 1 is equal to E
    and N is equal to B
    otherwise an exp M = E - 1
    and the power for B with M is a number K
    and N = B * K.

the p for a terms is the amount of the principal of the terms.

the r for a terms is a number if
    the monthly rate for the terms is the number.

the n for a terms is the number of installments of the terms.

the compound factor for a terms is a number if
    the r for the terms is a number M
    and a base B = 1 + M
    and the n for the terms is a value
    and the power for B with the value is the number.

the payment for a terms is a number N if
    the p for the terms is a value V
    and the r for the terms is a number M
    and the compound factor for the terms is a number K
    and the compound factor for the terms is a number Q
    and N = V * (M * K) / (Q - 1).

